{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1198311-origination-of-the-fae","id":1198311,"title":"Origination of the Fae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-22T06:43:10-07:00","id":1198311,"title":"Origination of the Fae","content":"Ok. The True Fae in the 1e books I've read are primordial creatures that may or may not have been concurrent with the mythical Atlantis (Mage uber alis, etc.), and certainly entered Arcadia or sprung from it before recorded human history of the present timeline. Probably even, the True Fae have multiple origins.<br /> <br /> Certainly however they exist as creatures that lack human creativity and morals, either having given up such in contracts with Arcadia that bestow their immense, flexible power, or having never had it by virtue of never being remotely human.<br /> <br /> We also know that a Changeling with a high enough Wyrd (10+) can effectively drift off and join Arcadia as a new True Fae, after which point the supposition is that they lose whatever is left of their human soul and are complete creatures of the Wyrd. Eventually. Which is a silly word to use around Arcadia, but I'll do so anyway.<br /> <br /> So, what can we do to blend or bend this, without breaking things, to reflect legends we have:<br /> * The Tuatha de danann as a bronze-aged people who &quot;retreated under the hills&quot; and became faeries?<br /> * Morgan (le Fey) who went from being a girl to a nun to a queen to a witch to (by the time of late Medieval romances) a literal faerie seducing away brave knights such as Ogier.<br /> <br /> These are examples off the top of my head that don't seem to match the mortal-&gt;durance-&gt;Changeling-&gt;True Fae path laid out by the gameline. It seems more like they skip directly from mortal to some form of faerie investment, to (at the very least) a True Fae playing at significant echoes of their former humanity. Possibly, even, True Fae with real shreds of their humanity clinging... like the tatters of the King.<br /> <br /> So have I missed something? Does the game already capture alternative paths to faerie... um, investment? Somehow? If not, what would be a plausible mechanism by which another mortal or supernatural could set foot on such a path?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T06:48:48-07:00","id":1198314,"title":"","content":"I think 1e had \u201cpossible origins\u201d stuff for where the True Fae came from - not all of them require humanity as a starting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T08:07:39-07:00","id":1198324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1198311-origination-of-the-fae?p=1198314#post1198314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think 1e had \u201cpossible origins\u201d stuff for where the True Fae came from - not all of them require humanity as a starting point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, everything up to and including spontaneous generation. The question is, assuming a point of humanity, how to get to Fae status?<br /> <br /> Let's suppose that of existing Fae at any given point, some proportion of them have non-human origins. The rest, do--at minimum they were Changelings, once. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T09:03:54-07:00","id":1198336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1198311-origination-of-the-fae?p=1198324#post1198324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, everything up to and including spontaneous generation. The question is, assuming a point of humanity, how to get to Fae status?</div> </div> </div> </div>Trade. Highly metaphorical trade, in some cases, but trade nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Change is transactional where the Wyrd is concerned, and the means by which a &quot;new&quot; Fae is born need not be &quot;born from nothing into the forests of Arcadia.&quot; Very gradual deals with a place of highly variable time can result in some extreme transformations, especially when that place draws upon Vice and esoteric knowhow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T09:08:50-07:00","id":1198339,"title":"","content":"In other words, sufficiently long-term exposure to the Land of Faerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T09:24:46-07:00","id":1198341,"title":"","content":"While trade is a very likely theory, allow me to offer an alternative- it was theft. The Gentry were not, after all, the original inhabitants of Arcadia. The Land Under Hill has existed long before humanity- the True Fae were simply the ones to tame it, to steal it. They took the hearts of its kings and used them to write a story of their own liking. <br /> <br /> The Huntsmen were there first, and we all know, they do not bargain. The only law they follow is the law of the Wild Hunt- and if you wish to crown yourself upon them, you better show your self worthy by stealing their own bleeding heart.<br /> <br /> (sure, things are different now- but that's the way I like to think everything began)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T09:48:23-07:00","id":1198346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1198311-origination-of-the-fae?p=1198339#post1198339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, sufficiently long-term exposure to the Land of Faerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even. The ascendancy of hobgoblin lords to the thrones of Faerie is apocryphal, but &quot;uncatchable notorious individual with strange habits&quot; is a loose subclass of legendary figure for a reason. The Wyrd is pervasive, and it's possible to cut a deal without ever speaking the words &quot;for this I forsake my humanity&quot; aloud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T09:56:17-07:00","id":1198349,"title":"","content":"We could trace several probable immigrations of &quot;True Fae&quot;. I'll use some purely arbitrary naming in order to facilitate discussion.<br /> <br /> 1. Huntsmen -- seized the commanding heights of Arcadia as representations of primordial factors necessary for physical survival--such as hunting food and consuming it; you could look at them as subsisting originally on the dreams of wild things if you wish.<br /> 2. Gentry -- stole the Huntsmen's place at the top of Arcadia and cut deals with everything except Iron to cement their power.<br /> 3. Old gods -- (Tuatha, etc.) cut deals with the Wyrd, piggybacked on Gentry contracts and otherwise bought their way into power.<br /> 4. &quot;True&quot; Fae -- Came in contact with the Wyrd enough that it rubbed away their souls and filled them with something... else; Changelings whose high Wyrd rating draws them back into the Hedge permanently fall into this category, as do other Hedge-critters who find a way to acquire enough of the nature of the rulers of Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Notes:<br /> On 1... this is supposition on my part. Obviously the question is begged &quot;seized from what?&quot; It's turtles all the way down....<br /> On 2... I like to imagine the Gentry inhabited the Supernal, and were refugees from the Exarch's coup, even if they have acquired such a soaking in essential mannerisms and traits that they seem to consist of only fundamental story elements.<br /> On 4... Realize that thanks to the mutable and non-linear nature of time in Arcadia, your Keeper could in fact be a Changeing-come-True Fae who was kidnapped centuries in your future and subsequently evolved to high Wyrd.<br /> <br /> And again on the non-linear time business: since Arcadia can effectively lack time except when it <i>has to </i>have it, all influxes of new Fae happen at once, all the time.<br /> <br /> Correct me please on any of this.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 03-26-2018, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T10:00:22-07:00","id":1198352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1198311-origination-of-the-fae?p=1198346#post1198346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyrd is pervasive, and it's possible to cut a deal without ever speaking the words &quot;for this I forsake my humanity&quot; aloud.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why, from a mundane mortal perspective, becoming even <i>aware</i> of the Darkness is incredibly dangerous--for at the same time, the Darkness becomes aware of you.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. Wherein &quot;Darkness&quot; is defined loosely as &quot;non-intrinsically benevolent supernatural elements and/or forces&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T14:51:56-07:00","id":1246758,"title":"","content":"I think I'll just point out that given the relationship between the Wyrd and Time, it is just as possible that the origins of the True Fae may have not yet happened just as much as they have already taken place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-25T18:15:17-07:00","id":1248908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1198311-origination-of-the-fae?p=1246758#post1246758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'll just point out that given the relationship between the Wyrd and Time, it is just as possible that the origins of the True Fae may have not yet happened just as much as they have already taken place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Michael Moorcock did a story on this where his survivors at the end of time are the demon lords faced by Elric and Corum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T08:28:48-07:00","id":1249145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwolf8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1198311-origination-of-the-fae?p=1248908#post1248908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Michael Moorcock did a story on this where his survivors at the end of time are the demon lords faced by Elric and Corum.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>&quot;You Either Die A Hero, Or You Live Long Enough To See Yourself Become The Villain&quot; </b><b>--Harvey Dent</b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">&quot;How could the greatest hero of the Wind Age, the king of Muirthemne during its Golden Age, become the greatest evil of our time?&quot; --Myth the Fallen Lords</span></span><br /> <br /> &quot;What has been will be again,<br /> what has been done will be done again;<br /> there is nothing new under the sun.&quot; --Ecclesiastes 1:9</b><br /> <br /> The cyclical nature of story is, I think, an essential element to bring into the fore if you're deal with questions such as the Fae present--since they are, after all, tales wrapped in stories about enigmas. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T16:06:31-07:00","id":1249557,"title":"","content":"I have a completely different theory, wholly set aside from current CtL lore, and rather based on historical settings. I'm curious about what you think of it.<br /> The general concept: The Fae are spirits of places and objects, created out of the energy of emotions (basically Glamour) for those places, not necessarily for the beings themselves.<br /> <br /> There are several instances, mainly in Nordic mythology, that after a farm, mine or ship has been built, it gains one or more guardian spirits - Fae. Not guardians that necessarily guards the people who live there, but rather the animals or the building itself.<br /> For the sake of simplicity, let's take the garden gnome, based upon a Swedish &quot;Tomte&quot;, as an example. The name &quot;Tomte&quot; itself comes from the Swedish word for &quot;lot&quot; or &quot;property&quot; - the place where a house or farm is built. It lives somewhere underground on the property and helps around the farm if you're nice to it, but if you neglect to care for the farm, stomp on the ground where it lives or talk ill of the tomte, it may hurt the animals, turn milk sour, or give you bad luck with the harvest.<br /> <br /> Now, imagine that the tomte didn't <b>come</b> to your property from somewhere else. Imagine that the tomte was <b>created</b> from the feelings in your hard work, blood, sweat and tears of building a life, giving the tomte its attributes and personality. Imagine that the local mountain troll was created from the hate, anger, fear and sorrow of the people who lost friends on the mountain trails. That the winged fairies were created from the wonder, glee and lack of morals of the children playing in the forest.<br /> <br /> Let's take it one step further: The king of the fairies comes from the feelings for the whole forest, while each fairy subject is a guardian of a separate place within that forest - a tree often climbed, a waterfall often revered. Each fairy effectively a child of the fairy king of that forest, only so powerful and complicated as the feelings held for its origin, and the king taking a share from each and every one.<br /> <br /> Let's take it another step: How do you as Fae gain more power? There are two obvious ways:<br /> 1. You make people feel more for the place. The mountain troll takes another life, cherished by many - let's say a beautiful young girl from the village nearby, or why not a princess? People fear the trail where <b>you</b> live even more and spread the word to others.<br /> 2. You gain guardianship over more places. This is where we get to contracts and dealings. The more land you hold as guardian, the more feelings you gain and the more powerful you become. With more land follows mantles, rights and titles. Does it start to sound familiar?<br /> <br /> This is where we get to changelings.<br /> Kidnapping a human and switching it out for a fetch is well motivated in CtL. I'm fine with those explanations. But why would a troll who <b>can</b> get babies change away her troll baby for a human one?<br /> Well, a troll baby hidden from the power games of the Fae is far safer than one within their reach. Just hide it in plain sight as a human. Other fae may try to bargain with the human baby you raise when it gets older, thinking it fae. It won't do them any good, however, since it doesn't own guardianship of any land. The troll child will stay in power as long as it holds ownership of its origin.<br /> <br /> Should one of the fae lose ownership of all its land, it will die the moment it runs out of energy.<br /> <br /> That's my headcanon for fae origins. I have no idea where to put Arcadia or the Hedge into this, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T19:39:47-07:00","id":1249596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spinnerling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1198311-origination-of-the-fae?p=1249557#post1249557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general concept: The Fae are spirits of places and objects, created out of the energy of emotions (basically Glamour) for those places, not necessarily for the beings themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That...sounds a bit more like Changeling: the Dreaming over in WoD, not so much CtL.<br /> <br /> Dreaming leans a bit more into fae being the direct result of the dreams and emotions of humanity much more then what Lost does. Since in Lost, the True Fae tends to be framed as taking from humanity's dreams and making it fit within their slice of Arcadia, not so much being born out of humanity's dreams and emotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T06:03:56-07:00","id":1250233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1198311-origination-of-the-fae?p=1249596#post1249596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That...sounds a bit more like Changeling: the Dreaming over in WoD, not so much CtL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Spirits from the Hisil to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T09:36:53-07:00","id":1250262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1198311-origination-of-the-fae?p=1250233#post1250233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like Spirits from the Hisil to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, and while that's a very functional model, in CofD it's already taken of course. Spirits are voracious predators, generated by and feeding from the Essence created through places, actions and emotions. This is... kinda cool in a Princess Mononoke sorta way until they get hungry enough to reach across and try to <i>create </i>the stuff they like to eat. Then people become objects to farm at best and hollow out into little inhuman factories at worst. That's... that's horrifying.<br /> <br /> The Fae are... Others. They have limited creativity but all the stories from time and space to draw on if they bother to go out and get what they need. This also makes them bored and bored entities are prone to whimsy and idle mischief--especially directed against things weaker than they. Like people. It's not clear that the Fae <i>need </i>specific human emotions--Glamour--for food, but they do <i>like </i>the stories that humans create and charge with the emotion of myth. In the long run they rely on <i>those</i> stories for the foundations of their identities and are not above farming humanity by creating the conditions for stories big and small. All of which, based on the circular principle, are reflections of themes that have come before. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}